# License

The Skills & Practices Framework is offered under **two licenses**, because the
repository holds two different kinds of things: the framework **data and writing**, and
the **code** that builds and publishes it.

## The data and writing — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)

Everything under `data/`, everything under `docs/`, and the `README.md` is licensed under
**CC BY 4.0**. You are free to share and adapt it, including for commercial use, as long
as you give appropriate credit to Tech Fleet.

- Full legal text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
- Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
- `SPDX-License-Identifier: CC-BY-4.0`

## The code — Apache License 2.0

Everything under `tools/` and `schema/`, and any client packages, is licensed under the
**Apache License, Version 2.0**.

- Full legal text: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
- `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0`

## In plain terms

- **The framework itself (data and words):** use it anywhere, just credit Tech Fleet.
- **The tools and schemas (code):** use them freely under Apache-2.0.
- **Not sure which applies?** Data and writing are CC BY 4.0; scripts and schemas are Apache-2.0.

> Before the public launch, the full legal text of both licenses will be pasted into this
> repository so GitHub displays each one automatically.
